{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/8", "id": 5094866689, "node_id": "PR_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABL61_AQ", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/8", "diff_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/8.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/8.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/8", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/8/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/8/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/8/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/statuses/6b449d611eb8d6c20063d4e1729b1e3e3f3abc65", "number": 8, "state": "closed", "locked": false, "title": "Reach UP and SMP performance parity", "user": {"login": "gmkurtzer", "id": 13984965, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTg0OTY1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13984965?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "## Summary\n\n- distribute Linux runtime workers across available application CPUs\n- add a fast path for single remote thread yields\n- coordinate futex wait/wake behavior across SMP workers\n- implement Linux futex bitset masks and absolute timeout semantics\n- retain focused SMP correctness regressions and publish matched benchmark evidence\n\n## Performance\n\nRatios compare Rocky on Ginux with the matched Rocky on Linux control. Values above `1.00x` favor Ginux.\n\n| Topology | CPU | Memory | Threads | Mutex |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 CPU / 1 thread | 2.185× | 2.342× | 1.312× | 2.163× |\n| 2 CPU / 1 thread | 0.982× | 1.122× | 2.995× | 1.066× |\n| 4 CPU / 1 thread | 1.002× | 1.101× | 2.912× | 1.036× |\n| 2 CPU / 2 threads | 1.186× | 1.207× | 4.090× | 1.070× |\n| 4 CPU / 4 threads | 1.173× | 1.138× | 2.583× | 0.970× |\n\nEvery result meets the accepted `0.96×` parity floor, and 18 of 20 results exceed the matched Linux median. Each cell contains nine Linux and nine Ginux samples using the same pinned sysbench binary and matched QEMU resources.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make check`\n- `make architecture-check`\n- `make test-smp`\n- `make test-rocky-smp-futex`\n- `make test-rocky-smp-shared-page`\n- `make test-rocky-smp-thread-context`\n\nDetailed evidence is recorded in `docs/feedback-hardening/GATE-12-PERFORMANCE-PARITY.md` and `docs/feedback-hardening/gate-12-results/`.\n", "labels": [], "milestone": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "created_at": "2026-10-31T05:26:26Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T05:29:49Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-31T05:28:14Z", "merged_at": "2026-10-31T05:28:14Z", "merge_commit_sha": "22d20a63544855148992e20d27d71c0e42f319d2", "assignee": null, "assignees": [], "requested_reviewers": [], "requested_teams": [], "head": {"label": "gmkurtzer:codex/performance-parity", "ref": "codex/performance-parity", "repo": {"id": 1413787216, "node_id": "R_kgDOVESuUA", "name": "ginux", "full_name": "gmkurtzer/ginux", "owner": {"login": "gmkurtzer", "id": 13984965, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTg0OTY1", "avatar_url": "https://ava